</description>

<solution>
Using $\log_2(a^b\cdot\text{constant})$ properties:
- $\log_2(yz)\cdot\log_2 x = \log_2(2^8\cdot 3^4) = 8 + 4\log_2 3$, giving $(a+b)c = 8 + 4t$
- $\log_2(zx)\cdot\log_2 y = \log_2(2^9\cdot 3^6) = 9 + 6\log_2 3$, giving $(b+c)a = 9 + 6t$  
- $\log_2(xy)\cdot\log_2 z = \log_2(2^5\cdot 3^{10}) = 5 + 10\log_2 3$, giving $(a+c)b = 5 + 10t$
</solution>

<result>
The system: $(a+b)c = 8+4t$, $(b+c)a = 9+6t$, $(a+c)b = 5+10t$ where $a,b,c,t > 0$.
